    "narrative": "The Austin Waves look for high-floor production today, led by **Gunnar Henderson** (71.95) and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (67.47). **Gunnar Henderson** remains our most essential start, as his matchup against Gausman is mitigated by a 100% stolen base expectation driven by Gausman\u2019s notoriously slow delivery, providing us that crucial speed edge we crave. **Kyle Tucker** (66.74) and **Jackson Merrill** (64.07) follow close behind; while **Jackson Merrill** faces a moderate hurdle with a sub-1.9s pop-time catcher and a pitcher adept at holding runners, his optimal #2 lineup spot and significant platoon advantage over Brazob\u00e1n keep his scoring ceiling high. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (64.40) also benefits from a favorable platoon split, capitalizing on Soroka\u2019s vulnerability to left-handed bats.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision today involved **Nolan Schanuel** (44.18), who narrowly missed the starting cut. While **Nolan Schanuel** projects as a functional utility piece, his matchup against Sheehan\u2014an arm with a sharp 3.31 xERA\u2014suppressed his efficiency score just below the threshold of our primary starters. We opted to prioritize the platoon advantages provided to **Curtis Mead** and **Josh Jung**, whose respective matchup data offered a higher probability of contributing to our core categories. We remain cautious with **Miguel Andujar** (43.10), as his score sits precariously near our 40.0 \"Below Floor\" limit; he stays in the lineup only due to positional availability, but he is a candidate for an early hook if his plate appearances prove unproductive against Brazob\u00e1n. All managers should monitor for late-breaking lineup changes, as any movement out of the top third of the order for our marginal starters like **Liam Hicks** (46.39) or **Miguel Vargas** (48.25) would effectively strip their remaining value for this daily cap cycle.",
